\subsection{Method \code{pi_mean()}}{
Prediction interval for a single future observation

Unified prediction-interval entry point supporting two modes:

\strong{Mode 1 -- single-sample (normal)}: pass a numeric vector \code{x}. The
interval has the form \verb{mean(x) +/- t_\{alpha/2, n-1\} * s * sqrt(1 + 1/n)},
i.e. the classical PI for one future observation from the same normal
population.

\strong{Mode 2 -- model-based}: pass a fitted \code{lm} model (or \code{formula} +
\code{data} to fit one internally) together with \code{newdata}. The interval
wraps \code{stats::predict(model, newdata, interval = "prediction")} per
the STAT_ANALYSIS_PLAN "pi_mean (封装 predict(interval='prediction'))"
requirement. One row of \code{newdata} produces one PI; multiple rows are
returned as a data frame in \code{result$prediction_table}.
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{IntervalAnalyzer$pi_mean(
  x = NULL,
  model = NULL,
  formula = NULL,
  data = NULL,
  newdata = NULL,
  conf_level = 0.95,
  alternative = "two.sided"
)}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{x}}{Numeric vector of sample observations (Mode 1). Ignored in
Mode 2 when \code{model} / \code{formula} is supplied.}

\item{\code{model}}{Optional fitted \code{lm} object (Mode 2). Takes precedence
over \code{formula}.}

\item{\code{formula}}{Optional formula (Mode 2). Used with \code{data} to fit an
internal \code{lm} when \code{model} is not supplied.}

\item{\code{data}}{Optional data frame (Mode 2). Required when \code{formula} is
given without \code{model}.}

\item{\code{newdata}}{Optional data frame of predictor values (Mode 2).
Defaults to the model frame (in-sample prediction).}

\item{\code{conf_level}}{Confidence level.}

\item{\code{alternative}}{Direction: \code{"two.sided"} (default), \code{"less"},
\code{"greater"}. For Mode 2 only \code{"two.sided"} is meaningful and other
values are coerced with a warning.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
